.TH CLOUDINIT 1
.SH NAME
cloudinit \- configure a cloud instance's network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cloudinit
[
.B -v
]
[
.BI -m " metadataip"
]
[
.BI -n " nifc"
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Cloudinit
binds the IP stack into
.BR /net ,
attaches the first Ethernet interface that answers, takes a DHCP lease,
and adds a host route to the metadata service.
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B -v
Report each step.
.TP
.BI -m " metadataip"
The metadata service's address, routed explicitly.  The default is
.BR 169.254.169.254 .
.TP
.BI -n " nifc"
How many Ethernet interfaces to try.  The default is 3.
.PP
None of this can be done from a shell.
.B #I
has to be bound into
.B /net
before there is an IP stack; the interface that
.B /net/ipifc/clone
allocates lasts only while that file descriptor stays open, so the
process that configures it must hold it; and the metadata service is on
a link-local address that no lease covers, so it needs a route of its
own through the lease's gateway.
.PP
The lease is not released.  The
.B pc64dev
configuration's startup does release it, because it is testing the
exchange rather than keeping the address; an instance that means to
keep its address must not.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/cloudinit.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR cloudfs (4),
.IR hget (1),
.IR dhcp (8)
.SS "The off-link gateway"
Every route is added with an interface, which is the fifth field
.B add
accepts in
.BR /net/iproute .
That is not decoration.  A route carrying an interface is used as it
stands; a route without one has to find its interface, and
.B findipifc
in
.B /os/inferno/ip/ipifc.c
will only match an interface whose subnet contains the gateway.
.PP
Compute Engine hands out a /32 netmask with the gateway outside it \(em
10.128.0.25/32 with gateway 10.128.0.1 \(em so no interface's subnet
contains it, every gateway route is unusable, and the instance can
reach nothing at all.  Linux's client is expected to cope with the same
thing by installing a link-scope route to the gateway before a default
route through it; naming the interface is how that is said here.
.SH BUGS
.IR Ping (1)
to the gateway is lost on Compute Engine whether or not routing works,
because ICMP to it is dropped there.  It is not a test of reachability
on that network, and reading it as one cost an afternoon.
.PP
Only DHCP.  An instance with a static address configured out of band is
not handled.
